{{template "advance_preamble" .}}

Resolve tech debt {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

Category: {{.category}} | Severity: {{.severity}}{{if .effort_estimate}} | Effort: {{.effort_estimate}}{{end}}

Check for existing resolution: review `git status` and `git diff`. If a refactor + regression tests exist and the quality gate passes, advance immediately.

---

LOAD: implementation skill, refactoring skill, test-driven-development skill.

READ:
(1) Tech debt body at {{.file_path}}
(2) Prior notes: `shark td notes {{.id}}` — pay special attention to any `decision`-type note named "Resolution plan" (the investigation output). If no such note exists, this debt was triaged directly to resolution as TRIVIAL — infer the plan from the TD body itself and proceed conservatively.
(3) Related entities: `shark links {{.id}}` — `shark get <key>` on any that touch the affected code
(4) `reference`-type notes — they may contain file:line pointers from investigation
(5) CLAUDE.md for coding standards and the mandatory quality gate

IMPLEMENT — regression-test-first workflow:

Step 1 — PROTECT existing behavior:
- For each code path the refactor touches, write a test that exercises the current behavior end-to-end.
- Run the new tests against the unchanged code — they MUST pass. This locks in the current contract.
- If you cannot write such a test (untestable seam), STOP and add a `blocker`-type note: `shark td note add {{.id}} --type=blocker --content="Cannot write regression test for <path> because <reason>"` then `shark status set {{.id}} blocked --reason "Untestable seam"`.

Step 2 — REFACTOR underneath the tests:
- Apply the resolution plan.
- Keep changes scoped to the tech debt — no drive-by edits, no unrelated cleanup.
- Run the regression tests after each meaningful change; they must stay green.

Step 3 — QUALITY GATE (MANDATORY):
```bash
make fmt && make lint && make test
```
Fix ALL failures before advancing. No exceptions.

Step 4 — RECORD the resolution:
- `shark td note add {{.id}} --type=implementation --content="<summary of what changed, which files, why this is now better>"`
- If you uncovered follow-up tech debt or future work, capture it: `shark td note add {{.id}} --type=future --content="..."` or `/triage` a new entity.

EXIT GATE:
- Regression tests exist and prove behavior is preserved
- Refactor matches the resolution plan (no scope creep)
- Quality gate passes
- An `implementation`-type note describes the change
- {{template "advance" .}} (goes to `ready_for_code_review`)
